The lookup is built in **`gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/internal/bind/EnumTypeAdapter.java`**.

Specifically, in the private constructor `EnumTypeAdapter(Class<T> classOfT)` (lines 64–111), the `nameToConstant` map is populated per enum constant field, and the `@SerializedName` handling — including its `alternate()` values — happens at lines 95–101:

```java
SerializedName annotation = constantField.getAnnotation(SerializedName.class);
if (annotation != null) {
  name = annotation.value();
  for (String alternate : annotation.alternate()) {
    nameToConstant.put(alternate, constant);
  }
}
nameToConstant.put(name, constant);
```

This is the map `read()` (line 120) consults via `nameToConstant.get(key)` when deserializing, so this is the spot to fix the alternate-name handling.

The file is:

**`gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/internal/bind/EnumTypeAdapter.java`**

Specifically its constructor (lines 64–111) builds `nameToConstant`. I can see the actual bug too, at lines 95–101:

```java
SerializedName annotation = constantField.getAnnotation(SerializedName.class);
if (annotation != null) {
  name = annotation.value();
  for (String alternate : annotation.alternate()) {
    nameToConstant.put(alternate, constant);
  }
}
nameToConstant.put(name, constant);
```

The loop putting `alternate` names into `nameToConstant` runs **before** the enum constant's own primary field name (`constant.name()`, i.e. the Java identifier) is ever put in the map — the primary key inserted afterward is `annotation.value()` (the serialized name), not `constant.name()`. So looking up an enum by its alternate `@SerializedName` works fine (that part's actually correct), but the constant's original Java field name is never registered when a `@SerializedName` annotation is present, since `name` was reassigned to `annotation.value()` before the `nameToConstant.put(name, constant)` call — losing the ability to deserialize by the enum's own identifier when it also has `@SerializedName`. That's the file/spot to fix.

**File:** `gson/src/main/java/com/google/gson/internal/bind/EnumTypeAdapter.java`

The `nameToConstant` map (and its sibling `stringToConstant`/`constantToName` maps) that back enum deserialization are built in `EnumTypeAdapter`'s private constructor (lines 64–111). It reflects over the enum's declared fields, and for each constant checks for a `@SerializedName` annotation (lines 95–104):

```java
SerializedName annotation = constantField.getAnnotation(SerializedName.class);
if (annotation != null) {
  name = annotation.value();
  for (String alternate : annotation.alternate()) {
    nameToConstant.put(alternate, constant);
  }
}
nameToConstant.put(name, constant);
```

This is the single place to fix the alternate-name deserialization bug.
